## 3. Fix repo prerequisites first (small, do these before Jenkins)

These are the honest gaps a pipeline would trip on. None require real app work.

| Gap | Suggestion |
|---|---|
| **No `package-lock.json`** | Run `npm install` once in `backend/` and commit the lockfile. Docker builds become reproducible and `npm ci` usable. (frontend/voter-simulator have no deps — skip.) |

The backend `Dockerfile` already copies `package*.json` before `src`, so the `npm install --omit=dev` layer stays cacheable — keep it that way (already the case ✅).

