## 5. GitHub ↔ Jenkins — make GitHub talk to your Oracle Jenkins

### 5.1 Tell Jenkins its own URL — `localhost` is correct here
**Manage Jenkins → System → Jenkins URL** = `http://localhost:8080`.

### 5.2 Webhook — skip unless the box gets a public IP
> **Not usable on this box:** the webhook needs GitHub (public internet) to reach Jenkins, which requires a public IP. Yours has none — use §5.3 instead.

### 5.3 Polling — the trigger to use (no inbound connection needed)
This works with no public IP: Jenkins reaches **out** to GitHub instead of GitHub reaching in. In the job, **Build Triggers → Poll SCM** with `H/3 * * * *` — Jenkins pulls the repo state every ~3 min and builds when `main` has new commits.

### 5.4 Job strategy
A single **Pipeline** job on `main`, pointing at the repo's `Jenkinsfile` (repo is public, so checkout needs no credentials; switch to a credentialed checkout if it ever goes private).

