## 6. Credentials + global env (Manage Jenkins → Credentials → System → Global)

All secrets live in **Jenkins** (never in the repo). Create these before the first green run to end:

| Credential ID | Kind | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `registry-credentials` | Username with password | **Docker Hub** username (`sachinmaskar`) + **Docker Hub access token** — used for `docker login` (§7.5) |
| `sonar-token` | Secret text | SonarQube token from §4.4 (already created — analysis is green) |
| `trivy-token` | Secret text | (optional) Trivy server token — **only if** the server started with `--token` (§4.5) |

The Jenkinsfile reads two **Environment variables** (no secrets here — set under **Manage Jenkins → System → Global properties → Environment variables**):

| Variable | Value | Required? |
|---|---|---|
| `TRIVY_SERVER_URL` | `http://<azure-vm-public-ip>:8082` | ✅ required |
| `TRIVY_TOKEN` | the server token, if any | only if the server has one |

**Create the Docker Hub access token first** (required before Stage 4/5/6 run): Docker Hub → **Account Settings → Security → New Access Token** (name e.g. `jenkins-ci`) → use the token as the **password** in `registry-credentials` (username `sachinmaskar`). A plain account password works too, but an access token lets you scope it and revoke it independently.

