## 10. Verification checklist (what "Phase 2 done" means)

- [ ] Commit to `main` → pipeline runs automatically (Poll SCM, within ~3 min)
- [ ] SonarQube analysis posts to the server; a deliberately bad change is caught
- [ ] Trivy stage contacts the **Azure VM server** — logs show the scan running server-side; no CRITICAL/HIGH (or a real finding blocked the push)
- [ ] Tagged images exist on Docker Hub: `sachinmaskar/voting:<svc>-<sha8>` + `:<svc>` for all 3 services
- [ ] `docker pull sachinmaskar/voting:backend && docker inspect` on any box returns the byte-identical image the pipeline just pushed (same sha8 → same digest)

Once these pass → tell the user **Phase 2 is verified**; only then plan Phase 3 (Terraform → EKS → Helm), which replaces the push-with-no-deploy tail of this pipeline with staging/prod deploy stages.
